PATCH 577: the AI's fire and weapon-select dispatches (a28c/a29b and their STRSEG tables), the four
weapon-spawn methods' AX, the fire-support request (aea6) and the objective-marker phase (b4fc).

board:0017.  Found by the self-play sweep after the time base (board:0026): SAUDI5 crashed in the AI's
turn, SAUDI3 never left its first cockpit frame.  Everything below is asm-verified against
re_out/fist_dat_image.bin; the two STRSEG tables against scratch/oracle/player.ram.bin (oracle
STRSEG 0x3e8d, 0x2082 <-> the port's 0x0f69 cluster).

  a28c   `mov gs,[0x70] ; mov bx,[di] ; shl bx,2 ; call DWORD gs:[bx+0x3131] ; ret` -- the unit's
         type word selects a FAR method in the STRSEG table {0f69:81ba, 8bb0, 92cb, a5c0} =
         FUN_1000_784a / 8240 / 895b / 9c50, the weapon-spawn methods, called with DI = the unit.
         Ghidra host-deref'd DI, read the table from DGROUP and called it near.  The caller b0be tests
         the AX they leave (`cmp al,0x4c ; test al,0x20`), so a28c now returns it.
  a29b   `.. shl bx,1 ; jmp WORD gs:[bx+0x3141]` -- the near table {7e87, 89fe, 921a, 9a04}, one per
         unit type, each `movzx bx,[di+0x91] ; add bl,2 ; cmp bl,6 ; jbe ; xor bl,bl` then
         `call 7963` / `lcall 0f69:892c` (FUN_1000_7fbc) / `0f69:94ec` (8b7c) / `0f69:9fbe` (964e), the
         per-type animation-state setters.  Ghidra saw no code at the four targets (they sit behind
         the 7e77 far table) and read the jump table as a host pointer; they are emitted here.
  784a/8240/895b/9c50  return AX: 0x27 on the spawn path (c047 keeps it unless DI is the audible unit
         [0x9fdf], then e2c2's op-0x64 result) and 0x3031 on the fail path (a4a2 preserves it).  8240
         (0f69:8bb0) and 9c50 (0f69:a5c0) are rebuilt like patch 495's 784a: `cmpb [di+0xfa],0 ; je
         fail ; decb ; push di ; ax=0x14 ; call b1df ; mov si,di ; pop di ; jb fail ; lcall 9a50 ;
         ax=0x27 ; lcall c047 ; clc ; retf` (9c50 has no ammo counter) -- Ghidra dropped b1df's
         projectile, the CF and DI (unaff_CS).
  aea6   (0f69:b816) the FIRE-SUPPORT request, b0be's `test al,0x20` branch: the side's battery count
         [0x9ccb]/[0x9ccd], the cooldown [0x9f17+bx] against [0x6cde], bf3c(4), the first battery with
         rounds ([si+0x1f]), then -- without a target [di+0x97] -- an aim point 0x9684 stepped 0x28
         times along the unit's heading (a192 -> 0459 with cx = [di+0x38], outputs << 6) until e1d1's
         terrain rises above its Z byte; the fire-mission slot (16 x 0xe at 0x9ce7 / 0x9dc7) gets
         {2, [0x6cde], target pos or the point}; 66cd(STRSEG:0x3193), bee2(0x29 / 0x2a), the cues
         0x2f0f / 0x2f40 / 0x2ef7.  Ghidra host-deref'd DI and the tables and lost 0459's outputs and
         e1d1's AX.
  b4fc   (0f69:be6c) c33c phase 1, the OBJECTIVE MARKERS of the cockpit view: gated on [0x6d2c]&2,
         [0x6dab]&2, [0xe6ef] < 2 and [0x1549] == 0x1e; emits one 0x34-byte record at the render
         cursor (`add di,2 ; stosw 0, 0x10, 0, 0 ; three dwords ; add di,0x1c ; the sprite word`),
         `clc` = found.  Ghidra wrote the record through a stack-residue pointer and dropped the CF
         and the cursor (g_fist_render_di, patch 310) -- SAUDI3 never left its first cockpit frame.

  Effect: SAUDI3, SAUDI5 resolve; the sweep's AZER4 / INDIA6 / UKRAINE7 needed the shim's interrupt
  frame as well (tools/native_main.c, same commit): the ISR's own carry leaked into the interrupted
  dispatch through g_fist_cf.

